/* ============================================================================
   MATERIAL ATLAS
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Flat-shaded coloured polygons are what made the first 3D pass look cheap next
   to the old sprite art: the sprites carried grain, panel lines, rivets, rust
   and wear, and untextured geometry threw all of that away. This puts it back
   as a real texture.

   An 11x10 grid of 256px tiles. Every tile is TILEABLE, and the shader takes
   fract() of the incoming UV before mapping it into its tile, so a long hull
   repeats its plating at a consistent physical size instead of stretching one
   copy across the whole surface.

   Tiles are luminance-ish and get multiplied by the vertex colour and the team
   tint, so one plating tile serves every painted surface in the game.
   ============================================================================ */
